# UI Toolkit (Unity style guide)

From [Unity's C# style guide](https://unity.com/resources/c-sharp-style-guide-unity-6). C# scripts: `unity-csharp-naming` + `unity-csharp-formatting`. **UXML/USS class names use BEM**, not C# PascalCase.

## UI Toolkit vs uGUI (Canvas)

**Default for Grid Dungeon:** **UI Toolkit** (`UIDocument`, UXML/USS, `VisualElement`) for player-facing HUD, menus, full-screen overlays (e.g. `ScreenFadePresenter`), and Editor tools ([`unity-editor-ui-toolkit.mdc`](unity-editor-ui-toolkit.mdc) in design-docs).

**Do not add new uGUI** (`UnityEngine.UI` — `Canvas`, `Image`, `Button`, legacy `Text`) without **explicit user approval**.

### Before implementing uGUI — ask first

If a task would use any of the following, **stop and ask the user** before coding. Propose a UITK approach and wait for confirmation:

- `Canvas`, `CanvasScaler`, `GraphicRaycaster`, `ScreenSpaceOverlay`
- `Image`, `RawImage`, `Mask`, uGUI `Text` / `Button`
- A second overlay stack that competes with existing `UIDocument` + `GamePanelSettings`

**UITK alternatives to suggest:** full-screen `VisualElement` + `style.backgroundColor` / opacity; shared `Assets/UI/Settings/GamePanelSettings.asset`; `UIDocument.sortingOrder` above HUD (e.g. screen fade at **10000**).

### When uGUI may be acceptable (still confirm with user)

- User explicitly requested uGUI for that feature
- Third-party asset requires uGUI and has no UITK path (state why in code or PR)
- Touching legacy uGUI already in scene — prefer migrating to UITK unless user scopes a uGUI-only fix

### Project examples (UITK)

| Feature | Approach |
|---------|----------|
| Exploration / Hub / Combat HUD | `UIDocument` + UXML under `Assets/UI/Screens/` |
| Screen fade | `ScreenFadePresenter` on child `ScreenFade` — UITK overlay, not `Image` |
| Editor tools | UITK `CreateGUI` — see design-docs `unity-editor-ui-toolkit.mdc` |

## Separation of concerns

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **UXML** | Structure, hierarchy, `name` hooks for queries — minimal inline style |
| **USS** | Layout, colors, states, responsive rules |
| **C#** | Behaviour, data binding, events — `MonoBehaviour` / presenter beside `UIDocument` |

Do not embed game logic in UXML. Do not hardcode colours in UXML when a USS class exists.

## No business logic in UXML

**UXML is markup, not authority.** Phase rules, roster state, shop prices, combat eligibility, and input-bind copy live in **C#** (presenters, coordinators, Core). UXML/USS only declare **where** nodes exist and **how** they look.

| Belongs in C# | Not in UXML |
|---------------|-------------|
| Show/hide by phase, tab, or overlay | Duplicate trees per phase (`hub-rail.uxml` + `combat-rail.uxml` for same shell) |
| Dynamic labels (HP, floor name, credits, row text) | Hardcoded player-facing copy that changes with game state |
| Which buttons exist and what they do | Static `Button` lists that only one screen ever uses — build into a shared host in code |
| Input bind strings | `Label` footers with `[Z] Confirm · [X] Cancel` (use `InputHints` + `TabbedPickerRailHints`) |
| Enable/disable, selected row, fullscreen | Inline `style="display: none"` toggles without a BEM `--hidden` class |

**Branching:** one **shell** UXML per reusable block; C# picks visible branch via **BEM modifier** (`EnableInClassList`) or populates an empty host (`PanelHost`, row list, tab strip). Do not fork UXML for every state — fork only when **layout structure** genuinely differs (e.g. `ItemListPickerLayout` profiles with different `name` hooks + `HiddenClass`).

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD — game-state copy and bind footer baked into markup -->
<ui:Label text="Floor 3 — buy stim_draft for 50c" />
<ui:Label text="[Z] Confirm · [X] Cancel" />

<!-- ✅ GOOD — stable hooks; presenter sets text / visibility -->
<ui:Label name="hub-credits" class="hub-hud__credits" text="—" />
<ui:VisualElement name="command-rail-panel" class="command-rail__panel" />
```

## Reusable shared components

New UI should **compose** existing shared blocks under `Assets/UI/Screens/Shared/` — not re-embed the same tree inside a phase HUD.

| Shared component | UXML / presenter | Reuse rule |
|------------------|------------------|------------|
| **Party menu overlay** | `PartyMenu.uxml`, `PartyMenuOverlayView` | Hub **Tab** and exploration **Esc** — same shell; phase hosts only open/close and publish hints |
| **Command rail** | `CommandRail.uxml`, `CommandRailPresenter` | One shell; hub / combat / party section rails populate `PanelHost` in code (`CommandRailPanelBuilder`, `RailMenuFocus`) |
| **Command rail info** | `CommandRailInfo.uxml`, `CommandRailInfoPresenter` | Non-button copy (titles, service lines) — not duplicated per phase UXML |
| **Global input hints** | `InputHint.uxml`, `InputHintPresenter` | One strip, `sortingOrder` 300 — phase views publish via `InputHints`; see `unity-global-input-hints.mdc` |
| **Tabbed item picker** | `ItemListPicker.uxml`, `ItemListPickerView` | Shared row/tab view; **hosts** use [ItemListInventory](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-services.md#item-list-inventory--itemlistinventorypresenter--itemlistinventory) service (standalone `UIDocument`) — not `CloneTree` on phase HUDs |
| **Item list inventory** | `ItemListInventoryOverlay.uxml`, `ItemListInventoryPresenter` | Hub shop, combat item, party bag — one facade; modal + rail offset; see `centralized-ui-services.mdc` |
| **Rail menu template** | `RailMenuVertical.uxml` | Empty host for new vertical rails — do not copy-paste rail markup |

**Before adding a new UXML file**, ask:

1. Does a shared component already cover this? → extend profile, modifier, or presenter instead.
2. Will a second screen need the same chrome for the initial release? → put it in `Shared/` with its own `UIDocument` + presenter ([centralized UI services](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-services.md)).
3. Is the difference only data or visibility? → C# + USS class toggle on one tree.

**Phase HUDs** (`HubHud`, `CombatHud`, `ExplorationHud`) orchestrate: bind events, call shared facades, toggle modifiers. They do **not** own cross-phase overlays inline in their UXML.

**Centralized services** (`ItemListInventory`, `InputHints`, `PartyFormationFloater`, …): one `UIDocument` per concern under `GameState`. **Do not** embed or geometry-dock service trees into phase UXML as the final integration — modal + `sortingOrder` + USS rail offset instead (`centralized-ui-services.mdc`).

Design reference: [shared menu & picker UI](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/shared-menu-picker-ui.md), [centralized UI services](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-services.md).

## BEM naming (UXML + USS classes)

Unity recommends **Block Element Modifier (BEM)** for classes in UXML and USS (same spirit as modern CSS).

Pattern: `block-name__element-name--modifier-name`

| Part | Meaning | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Block** | Standalone UI component | `combat-log` |
| **Element** | Part of a block (`__`) | `combat-log__entry` |
| **Modifier** | Variant/state (`--`) | `combat-log--collapsed`, `combat-log__entry--selected` |

Use **kebab-case** within each segment. A BEM name should convey **what** it is, **where** it lives, and **how** it differs from siblings.

- Apply BEM to **`class`** attributes in UXML and selectors in USS — not to C# type names.
- **UXML `name`** (for `Q()`): stable kebab-case id per element — may mirror the element segment (`combat-log__round` → `name="combat-log-round"`) but need not duplicate every modifier class.
- **C# types**: PascalCase — `CombatLogView`
- **Assets**: `CombatHud.uxml`, `CombatHud.uss`, `CombatHudView.cs`

## UXML

- One root screen / panel per primary UXML; reuse **templates** (`<ui:Instance>` / UXML templates) for repeated chunks.
- Assign every element you query in code a **`name`**; avoid querying by fragile class-only paths across refactors.
- Prefer **USS classes** over duplicated inline `style=""` attributes.

```xml
<!-- ✅ GOOD — BEM classes -->
<ui:VisualElement name="combat-log" class="combat-log">
    <ui:Label name="combat-log-round" class="combat-log__round" text="Round 1" />
    <ui:ScrollView class="combat-log__entries combat-log__entries--dense" />
</ui:VisualElement>
```

## USS

**Reminder:** USS is **not** full browser CSS — no `calc()`, limited selectors, flex-only layout. See [`unity-uitk-uss-limits.mdc`](unity-uitk-uss-limits.mdc) before assuming web CSS works.

- Selectors target **BEM classes** — `.combat-log { }`, `.combat-log__entry { }`, `.combat-log__entry--selected { }`
- **Theme / variables** for shared colours, spacing, fonts — `var(--spacing-md)` on blocks.
- Prefer **modifiers** (`--selected`, `--disabled`) over ad-hoc class names like `.selected-red`.
- Pseudo-states: `:hover`, `:active` on BEM blocks/elements where USS supports them.
- Keep selectors **shallow** — prefer one BEM class per node over long descendant chains.

## C# bindings

- Cache `VisualElement` / control references in `OnEnable` or after `rootVisualElement` is ready — no per-frame `Q` unless necessary.
- Subscribe in `OnEnable` / `RegisterCallback`, **unsubscribe** in `OnDisable` / `UnregisterCallback`.
- Toggle state with **BEM modifier classes** (`element.AddToClassList("combat-log__entry--selected")`) before inline styles.
- Custom controls: inherit `VisualElement`, use `UxmlElement` / `UxmlFactory` + `UxmlTraits` (Unity 6) for designer-friendly UXML.

### Prefer USS class toggles over `element.style` in C#

**Default:** layout, size, colour, visibility, and state styling live in **USS**. C# **toggles classes** (`EnableInClassList`, `AddToClassList` / `RemoveFromClassList`) — do **not** set `VisualElement.style` properties for those concerns unless an exception below applies.

| Do in USS + class toggle | Avoid in C# |
|--------------------------|-------------|
| Width / height / min-max size | `style.width = 336f`, `style.height = …` |
| Opacity, display, flex alignment | `style.opacity`, `style.display` (when a `--hidden` / `--fullscreen` modifier exists) |
| Colours, borders, padding | `style.backgroundColor`, `style.borderTopWidth`, … |
| **Hover/focus micro-states** (`:hover`, `menu-item--focused`) | Per-frame `style` writes for selection chrome |
| **Show/hide overlay motion** | USS `transition-property` + `schedule.Execute` duration hacks — use DOTween instead (below) |

**Show/hide transitions (overlays, panels, map layout settle):** drive motion with **`UiToolkitTweens`** + **`UiTransitionSession`** (`Assets/Scripts/Runtime/UI/`). Helpers: `PopInTransition`, `SlideTransition`, `CollapseTransition`, `CommandRailEnterTransition`, `CommandRailPanelTransition`, `RailInfoCopyTransition`, `MapViewPanelTransition`. Panel host repopulates go through **`CommandRail.SwapPanelContent`** — not ad-hoc `PanelHost.Clear` on phase HUDs. Toggle BEM modifiers for **steady end state**; tween via inline `style` during motion; `StyleKeyword.Null` on complete. **One duration source** — C# constants only; no matching `transition-duration` on those USS blocks. Edit Mode tests: `UiTransitionSession.CompleteImmediatelyForTests`.

**Pattern:** one active modifier per axis when values are discrete — e.g. `map-view--panel-cols-20`, `map-view--panel-rows-20`, `map-view--panel-cell-24`, `map-view__grid--cell-size-24`. Centralize toggles in a small helper (e.g. `MapViewLayoutClasses`) when many mutually exclusive classes exist.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — behaviour picks a USS modifier; stylesheet owns pixels and transitions
m_root.EnableInClassList("map-view--fullscreen", fullscreen);
MapViewLayoutClasses.SetPanelCellSize(m_root, cellSizePx);

// ❌ BAD — duplicates USS, blocks transitions, drifts from design tokens
m_root.style.width = 496f;
m_root.style.minWidth = 496f;
cell.style.width = cellSize;
```

**Inline `style` is OK when:**

- **Layout-derived coordinates** that USS cannot know ahead of time (e.g. marker `left` / `top` from `worldBound` / `MapGridOverlayAnchor`, or **DOTween `translate`** in `MapGridMarkerAnimator`). **Do not** put `left` / `top` / `translate` in USS `transition-property` on those markers — it fights step tweens and reads as stagger.
- **One-off Editor or dev tools** not worth a modifier matrix.
- **No stable discrete set** of values and adding dozens of USS classes would be noise — document why in a short comment.

For **hover/focus** modifier families only, USS `transition-property` on the base block is OK. Do **not** add USS transitions for orchestrated show/hide — use `UiToolkitTweens` instead.

```csharp
// naming: PascalCase type; query by kebab-case name matching UXML name=""
public class CombatHudView : MonoBehaviour
{
    Label m_roundLabel;

    void OnEnable()
    {
        var root = GetComponent<UIDocument>().rootVisualElement;
        m_roundLabel = root.Q<Label>("combat-log-round");
    }
}
```

## Command rail modal chip rail

When a **service or section chip** opens a child modal (hub Buy/Sell, Heal/Revive, party bag, combat skill picker), use **`CommandPanelModalSupport`** — do not hand-roll per-screen enable/selected logic.

| API | Use when |
|-----|----------|
| `SyncModalChipRail` | Hub service **action button pair** opens modal — binds `rail-menu__item--selected`, disables siblings |
| `ApplyModalChipEnables` | Multi-chip rail with nullable slots (party menu sections) |
| `SetModalOpen(host, open)` | Host `command-panel--modal-open` while child owns input |

Recipe: domain helper → `SetModalOpen` → `SyncModalChipRail` / `ApplyModalChipEnables` → `ClearFocusItems` on service rail while modal open. See design-docs [shared menu § Modal rail sibling disable](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/shared-menu-picker-ui.md#modal-rail-sibling-disable-commandpanelmodalsupport) and [centralized UI gotchas § Hub service modal chip rail](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-gotchas.md#hub-service-modal-chip-rail-commandpanelmodalsupportsyncmodalchiprail).

## Global input hints

**Input bind copy only** on `InputHintPresenter` (bottom-right strip) — not map legend, coords, or warnings. Publish via `InputHints`; constants in `TabbedPickerRailHints` (segment order: Z/X → Up/Down & Q/E → other keys). No duplicate bind footers on panels or pickers. See [`unity-global-input-hints.mdc`](unity-global-input-hints.mdc).

## Project layout (recommended)

```
Assets/.../UI/
  Settings/      — GamePanelSettings.asset (shared Panel Settings for UIDocument)
  Screens/       — feature UXML/USS pairs
  Themes/        — default Theme StyleSheet, tokens
  Scripts/       — views / presenters (under Assets/Scripts/UI/)
```

Align namespaces with folders (`GridDungeon.UI.Combat`). Match existing layout if the repo already defines one.

When editing legacy UI, match surrounding UXML/USS patterns unless refactoring that screen.
